      University of Perpetual Help System DALTA — Calamba Campus
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 11pt; color: #cbd5e1; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-weight: 600;">
      College of Engineering • Engineering Student Council (ESC) A.Y. 2026–2027
    </p>
    <h1>ENGINEERING DAYS 2026<br><span style="font-size: 15pt; color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400;">Student & Marshal QR Attendance Guide</span></h1>
    <table class="meta-table">
      <tr>
        <td style="width: 50%;"><strong>Event Dates:</strong> October 19–20, 2026 (Mon–Tue)</td>
        <td style="width: 50%;"><strong>Official Gate PIN:</strong> <span style="color: #fbbf24; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">2026</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Venues:</strong> UPHSD Gymnasium, Campus Oval & Engineering Labs</td>
        <td><strong>Roster Size:</strong> 588 Engineering Students (Track A)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2"><strong>Official Online Scanner:</strong> <a href="https://meodl.vercel.app/engday_scanner.html" style="color: #67e8f9; text-decoration: underline;">https://meodl.vercel.app/engday_scanner.html</a></td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="tip-box">
    <div class="alert-title" style="color: #1d4ed8;">Welcome Engineering Students & Student Marshals!</div>
    Welcome to <strong>Engineering Days 2026</strong>! To make gate entry, sports events, booth visits, and final certificates seamless and fair for all <strong>588 engineering students</strong>, our college utilizes an automated high-speed QR Attendance Pass system. This handbook contains everything you need to know about preparing your QR pass, entering and exiting venues, taking breaks, and operating the mobile gate scanners.
  </div>

  <!-- ========================================== -->
  <!-- 2. PART A: STUDENT ATTENDANCE GUIDE       -->
  <!-- ========================================== -->
  <h1 style="color: #0f172a; margin-top: 24pt;">PART A: Quick Guide for All Engineering Students</h1>
  <p>Follow these 4 simple steps to ensure your attendance is smoothly recorded throughout all 8 activity blocks on October 19 and 20.</p>

  <h3><span class="step-number">1</span> Step 1: Get & Prepare Your QR Pass</h3>
  <p>Every enrolled engineering student has been assigned a personalized QR Attendance Card. You can access your card through your department student representative or via the online card viewer.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Print or Save on Your Phone:</strong> You may present either your printed physical card or a high-quality screenshot saved on your smartphone.</li>
    <li><strong>Maximize Screen Brightness:</strong> Before reaching the gate marshal, please turn your phone screen brightness up to <strong>100%</strong>. This eliminates glare and allows the gate scanner to read your code in less than half a second!</li>
    <li><strong>Add to Favorites / Lock Screen:</strong> Save your QR image to your phone's "Favorites" album or set it as a temporary lock screen wallpaper for instant access.</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- VISUAL 1 INSERTION -->
  <div class="img-container">
    <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Visual 1: Sample Student QR Pass" />
    <div class="img-caption">Visual 1 — Sample Official Engineering Days 2026 Student QR Attendance Card (showing Student Name, Program, Roster Code, and QR Code)</div>
  </div>

  <h3><span class="step-number">2</span> Step 2: Scan on Entry (Check-In)</h3>
  <p>When entering the Gymnasium, Campus Oval, or Computer/Electronics laboratories:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Fall in line politely at the designated entrance gate.</li>
    <li>Hold your QR card or phone screen flat, approximately <strong>4 to 6 inches</strong> away from the marshal's camera viewfinder.</li>
    <li>Listen for the audible scanner chime/beep and look for the green verification banner on the marshal's screen.</li>
    <li>The marshal will verify your name and section, and you are immediately cleared to enter!</li>
  </ol>

  <h3><span class="step-number">3</span> Step 3: Scanning Out for Breaks or Exits (Check-Out)</h3>
  
  <div class="warning-box">
    <div class="alert-title" style="color: #b45309;">⚠️ CRITICAL ATTENDANCE RULE: 7 out of 8 Sessions Require Check-Out!</div>
    Except for the Day 1 Morning Registration (which is entry-only), <strong>all remaining 7 activity blocks require scanning OUT when you exit or leave the venue</strong>. Whenever stepping out for lunch, snacks, water, restroom visits, or room transfers, you <strong>MUST</strong> tap out with the Gate Marshal!
  </div>

  <p><strong>Why is Scanning Out Essential for Students?</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Accurate Attendance Hours:</strong> Scanning out accurately logs your active participation dwell time. This ensures your department clearance and Certificate of Participation hours are fully credited.</li>
    <li><strong>Safety & Headcount Verification:</strong> In case of emergency drills or venue capacity limits, the marshals and university safety officers know exactly how many students are inside the building.</li>
    <li><strong>Avoiding Cutting / Absent Flags:</strong> If you leave the venue without scanning out, your session status may be marked incomplete by the automated audit system.</li>
  </ol>

  <!-- VISUAL 3 INSERTION -->
  <div class="img-container">
    <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Visual 3: Check-In & Check-Out Verification Modal" />
    <div class="img-caption">Visual 3 — Check-In & Check-Out Verification Modal (showing Student Status, 1-Tap Check-Out button, Exit Reason selector, and 8-Checkpoint Stamp Card)</div>
  </div>

  <h3><span class="step-number">4</span> Step 4: Forgot, Lost, or Damaged Your QR Pass? Don't Panic!</h3>
  <p>If your phone battery drains completely, or if you accidentally left your printed card at home, our gate system has a built-in safety net:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Approach the Student Marshal at the gate and politely state your <strong>Last Name</strong> or your <strong>Student Code</strong> (e.g., <code>EE-001</code>, <code>CE-014</code>, <code>MEODL-0001</code>, <code>IE-005</code>, <code>CPE-020</code>, <code>ECE-008</code>).</li>
    <li>The marshal will tap the <strong>🔍 Manual Lookup</strong> tab on their scanner.</li>
    <li>They will type the first 3 letters of your surname or code, locate your verified roster record, and check you in manually in <strong>under 3 seconds</strong>!</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="success-box">
    <div class="alert-title" style="color: #15803d;">Summary: Quick Student Checklist for EngDays 2026</div>
    <ul style="margin-bottom: 0;">
      <li>[V] Screenshot your QR Pass and save it to your phone's Favorites.</li>
      <li>[V] Set your phone brightness to maximum before reaching the gate line.</li>
      <li>[V] Scan IN when entering each activity block.</li>
      <li>[V] Scan OUT whenever stepping out for lunch, restroom, or transfer to another venue.</li>
      <li>[V] Memorize your Student Code (e.g., <code>CE-014</code>) for instant 3-second Manual Lookup.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <!-- ========================================== -->
  <!-- 3. OFFICIAL 8-CHECKPOINT SCHEDULE TABLE    -->
  <!-- ========================================== -->
