  <!-- ========================================== -->
  <!-- 4. PART B: MARSHAL & ESC OFFICER GUIDE     -->
  <!-- ========================================== -->
  <h1 style="color: #0f172a; margin-top: 28pt;">PART B: Quick Guide for Student Marshals & ESC Officers</h1>
  <p>Student Marshals and ESC Committee Officers are responsible for operating the mobile gate scanners, assisting students, and safeguarding attendance records. This section outlines your scanning duties and emergency protocols.</p>

  <h2>1. Official System Links & Security Access PIN</h2>
  <p>All marshals should bookmark these links on their mobile phones and laptops:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>📱 <strong>Mobile Gate Scanner:</strong> <a href="https://meodl.vercel.app/engday_scanner.html" style="color: #2563eb; font-weight: bold;">https://meodl.vercel.app/engday_scanner.html</a><br>
    <em>(Use this link on smartphones at every entrance and exit gate.)</em></li>
    <li>💻 <strong>Live Attendance Dashboard (HQ Laptop):</strong> <a href="https://meodl.vercel.app/engday_attendance.html" style="color: #2563eb; font-weight: bold;">https://meodl.vercel.app/engday_attendance.html</a><br>
    <em>(Used at the main Secretariat table to monitor live campus headcounts and session tallies.)</em></li>
    <li>🪪 <strong>QR Card Batch Printer:</strong> <a href="https://meodl.vercel.app/print_cards.html" style="color: #2563eb; font-weight: bold;">https://meodl.vercel.app/print_cards.html</a><br>
    <em>(Used to reprint cards for replacement or late registrants.)</em></li>
    <li>🔑 <strong>Official Staff / Marshal PIN:</strong> <span style="font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13pt; font-weight: 700; background-color: #fef3c7; color: #b45309; padding: 2pt 8pt; border-radius: 4pt; border: 1px solid #f59e0b;">2026</span><br>
    <em>(Enter PIN 2026 when opening the scanner to unlock administrative controls.)</em></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Step-by-Step Gate Scanning Workflow</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Open Scanner & Authorize:</strong> Open the Scanner link in Chrome (Android) or Safari (iPhone). Type the 4-digit PIN <code>2026</code> and tap <strong>Allow Camera</strong> when prompted.</li>
    <li><strong>Select Session:</strong> Tap the current Day tab (Day 1 or Day 2) and tap the active session button (e.g. <code>🏐 D1 AM SPORTS</code>). Alternatively, tap <strong>⚡ Live Now</strong> which automatically picks the active event based on campus clock.</li>
    <li><strong>Aim & Frame:</strong> Point the camera viewfinder at the student's QR code. Ensure the code is inside the green corner brackets.</li>
    <li><strong>Use Zoom Controls for Quick Focus:</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Tap <strong>1.5x</strong> or <strong>2x</strong> zoom if the student's card is held a few steps back or has plastic laminated reflection.</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>🔄 Switch Camera</strong> if you need to alternate rear lenses.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Enable Auto-Scan During Queues:</strong> Tap <strong>⚡ Auto-Scan: ON</strong> during busy morning or evening rush hours. In Auto-Scan mode, the scanner automatically logs verified check-ins and check-outs in <strong>1 second</strong> without requiring manual confirmation taps!</li>
  </ol>

  <!-- VISUAL 2 INSERTION -->
  <div class="img-container">
    <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Visual 2: Mobile Gate Scanner" />
    <div class="img-caption">Visual 2 — Mobile Gate Scanner Interface (showing Camera Box, Day 1/Day 2 Tabs, Session Chips, Zoom Controls, Switch Camera, and Manual Lookup)</div>
  </div>

  <h2>3. Monitoring the Central Attendance Dashboard (HQ Station)</h2>
  <p>The Lead Marshal and Secretariat Officers monitor attendance on the primary laptop stationed at the Gymnasium HQ table:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Total Roster (588 Students):</strong> Confirms the full eligible student body enrolled in Track A.</li>
    <li><strong>Attended Today Scorecard:</strong> Displays cumulative count and percentage of students who have checked in at least once today.</li>
    <li><strong>Currently Inside Venue:</strong> Real-time headcount of students actively inside the building.</li>
    <li><strong>Out on Break:</strong> Real-time headcount of students temporarily outside for lunch, snacks, or lab transfers.</li>
    <li><strong>Print QR Cards & Backup Buttons:</strong> Quick access buttons at the top toolbar to generate replacement badges or download event-wide snapshots.</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- VISUAL 4 INSERTION -->
  <div class="img-container">
    <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Visual 4: Live Attendance Dashboard" />
    <div class="img-caption">Visual 4 — Live Attendance Dashboard (showing Headcount Scoreboard, KPI Stat Cards, and Checkpoint Live Table Breakdown)</div>
  </div>

  <h2>4. Offline Safety, Local Storage & Cloud Sync Protocol</h2>
  
  <div class="success-box">
    <div class="alert-title" style="color: #15803d;">🛡️ Zero-Data Loss Guarantee: Scans Work 100% Offline!</div>
    The mobile gate scanner is built with offline-first local memory. Even if the gymnasium Wi-Fi drops or your mobile data runs out, <strong>DO NOT STOP SCANNING!</strong> Your phone saves every single scan, timestamp, and exit reason safely in its internal browser storage.
  </div>

  <p><strong>End-of-Shift Backup & Sync Routine:</strong></p>
  <ol>
    <li>At the end of your marshal shift, tap the <strong>💾</strong> backup icon at the top of the scanner screen.</li>
    <li>Tap <strong>💾 Export Backup</strong> to download a standalone backup file (<code>.json</code>) directly to your phone's Downloads folder. This ensures you have an independent receipt of every scan made on your device.</li>
    <li>When connected to campus Wi-Fi or data, tap <strong>☁️ Save & Sync Now</strong> to upload all pending scans to the central HQ database.</li>
    <li>Notify the Lead Marshal at the Secretariat table that your station is synced.</li>
  </ol>

  <!-- VISUAL 5 INSERTION -->
  <div class="img-container">
    <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Visual 5: Quick Save & Cloud Sync Panel" />
    <div class="img-caption">Visual 5 — Quick Save & Cloud Sync Panel (showing Device Local Storage Health, 1-Tap Export Backup, and Cloud Sync Now buttons)</div>
  </div>

  <h2>5. Quick Fixes for Gate Marshals (Troubleshooting FAQ)</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 30%;">Common Situation</th>
        <th style="width: 70%;">Instant Solution (How to Fix in 10 Seconds)</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Camera displays black screen or opens selfie camera</strong></td>
        <td>
          1. Tap the <strong>🔄 Switch Camera</strong> button below the scanner box to cycle to your phone's primary rear camera lens.<br>
          2. Close any background apps using the camera (e.g. TikTok, Instagram, Messenger).<br>
          3. Tap the lock/tune icon 🔒 in your browser's URL address bar &gt; Permissions &gt; Ensure Camera is set to <strong>Allow</strong>.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Campus Wi-Fi or mobile data disconnects</strong></td>
        <td>
          <strong>DO NOT STOP SCANNING!</strong> The scanner operates completely offline. All scans are recorded on your phone. Continue checking students in and out normally. When internet resumes, tap <strong>☁️ Save & Sync Now</strong>.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Student's phone screen has intense glare or reflection</strong></td>
        <td>
          1. Ask the student to tilt their phone slightly (about 15 degrees) away from overhead gymnasium halogen lights.<br>
          2. Tap the <strong>1.5x</strong> zoom button on the scanner so you can scan from a comfortable 1-foot distance.<br>
          3. Remind the student to set their screen brightness to 100%.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>QR code is wet, folded, unreadable, or student lost phone</strong></td>
        <td>
          Tap the <strong>🔍 Manual Lookup</strong> tab at the bottom of the scanner. Type the student's surname or their Roster Code (e.g., <code>EE-001</code>). Tap <strong>Check-In</strong> or <strong>Check-Out</strong>. Total time: 3 seconds!
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Student accidentally taps or scans their code twice</strong></td>
        <td>
          The scanner includes automated rapid-scan cooldown protection. Duplicate scans within 3 seconds are safely ignored and will show a polite notification on screen without double-counting the student.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>End of shift or battery low</strong></td>
        <td>
          Before handing off your station to the incoming marshal, tap <strong>💾 Export Backup</strong> to download a file copy. Never clear your browser history or close your tabs until the final day tallies are verified by the ESC President.
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

